; rdm_responder.loom
; An RDM responder (ANSI E1.20, Remote Device Management over DMX512) on
; an RS-485 half-duplex line: it finds RDM packets among the DMX512
; packets, checks their checksum, takes part in discovery (DISC_UNIQUE_
; BRANCH, DISC_MUTE, DISC_UN_MUTE), answers GET DEVICE_INFO and GET / SET
; IDENTIFY_DEVICE, NACKs what it does not support, turns the line round
; with a DE pin as a real responder does, and reports every packet meant
; for it to the host. RX comes from the RO output of an RS-485 transceiver,
; TX goes to its DI input and DE to its driver enable (1 = drive the line).
;
; Written on 2026-11-07, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). It needs the M2 core (pins,
; deadlines, timed waits, NOW, the FIFOs), LD/ST of slice B (SEMANTICS
; 6.11, built for the I2C EEPROM's array) for the packet buffer, and the
; bit engine's shift register in manual mode (SEMANTICS 6.9, built for the
; synchronous serial programs and USB's and CAN's encoders): SHI samples
; each received data bit and SHO sends the eleven bits of each 8N2 slot.
; No hardware knows DMX, RDM or even a UART: break detection, the slots,
; the additive checksum both ways, the UID match, the discovery range test,
; the encoded-UID reply, the parameter handlers, the responder delay and
; the DE turn-around are all firmware.
;
; Specification: ANSI E1.20 (RDM). tools/protomodels/rdm.py is the
; reference model written from it and cites each figure used here. The
; standard itself could not be fetched (ESTA's TSP refused the download):
; the timings come from the Open Lighting Project's code documentation,
; which quotes E1.20's tables by line, and are marked so in the model.
; The E1.20 section numbers in this file are from memory, unchecked.
;
; Pins: RX = IN0, TX = OUT0 (idle high: mark), DE = OUT1 (1 = drive the
; line), IDENT = OUT2 (high while IDENTIFY_DEVICE is on: the "identify"
; lamp). All four move with the assembler's --pin.
;
; Host command (INQ[0]), once, after RUN: the responder's UID, three words,
; most significant first: the manufacturer ID, then the device ID's high
; and low halves. DEVICE_INFO's 19 bytes (below, one per word at DEVINFO)
; are loaded with the image; the host may change them before RUN.
;
; Report (OUTQ[0]), per RDM packet with a good checksum that is addressed
; to this UID or broadcast (all devices, or this manufacturer's):
;     word 1    bits 15:8 the command class, bits 7:0 the flags:
;               bit 0  a response was sent (break, ACK or NACK)
;               bit 1  a DISC_UNIQUE_BRANCH response was sent (no break)
;               bit 2  the response was a NACK
;               bit 3  broadcast
;               bit 4  IDENTIFY_DEVICE is on (after the packet)
;               bit 5  muted (after the packet)
;     word 2    the parameter ID
; and a lone word 0x0080 for an RDM packet whose checksum is wrong or
; whose message length does not match its parameter data length. Packets
; for other UIDs and DMX512 packets of other start codes (dimmer data
; included) are ignored and not reported. A word that finds OUTQ full is
; dropped: the responder never stalls.
;
; Responses, E1.20 sections 6 and 7 (the model cites them):
;     DISC_UNIQUE_BRANCH  unmuted and lower bound <= UID <= upper bound:
;                         seven 0xFE, 0xAA, the UID's six bytes each sent
;                         as (b | 0xAA, b | 0x55), the checksum of those
;                         twelve bytes encoded the same way; no break
;     DISC_MUTE, UN_MUTE  muted / unmuted; to this UID: ACK, a control
;                         field of 0x0000
;     GET DEVICE_INFO     ACK, the 19 bytes
;     GET IDENTIFY        ACK, one byte 0 or 1
;     SET IDENTIFY        0 or 1: ACK, no data, and IDENT follows it;
;                         other values NACK NR_DATA_OUT_OF_RANGE
;     other parameters    NACK NR_UNKNOWN_PID (NR_UNSUPPORTED_COMMAND_CLASS
;                         for SET DEVICE_INFO); NR_FORMAT_ERROR for a
;                         wrong data length; NR_SUB_DEVICE_OUT_OF_RANGE for
;                         a sub-device other than the root (0xFFFF too,
;                         except for SET)
; Broadcast packets are acted on and never answered, except DISC_UNIQUE_
; BRANCH, which is always broadcast.
;
; Rate: eight ticks a bit. The host sets TICK_INT = 25, TICK_FRAC = 0
; before RUN (3.125 MHz at 50 MHz: 200 clocks, 4 us, a bit). The deadline
; pairs are proved for that tick (.tick below).
;
; Timing (the figures and the tables they come from are in the model):
;   - Receive (Table 3-3 line 1): a low run of 175 ticks (87.5 us) or more
;     is a break; the mark after break is not checked. Slots are sampled
;     as in dmx_fixture, 4 ticks into the start bit and 8 apart; a slot
;     must start within 2.1 ms (4200 ticks) of the last one, or the packet
;     is dropped. A break inside a packet starts a new one.
;   - Responder delay (Table 3-4, 176 us .. 2 ms): the response's first
;     falling edge (its break, or a DUB response's first start bit) comes
;     DELAY ticks after the middle of the request's last first stop bit:
;     200 us after the end of the request's last slot, to within a tick.
;   - DE rises one bit (4 us) before that first edge and falls at the end
;     of the response's last stop bit.
;   - The response (Table 3-1): break 46 bits (184 us, 176 .. 352), mark
;     after break 4 bits (16 us, 12 .. 88), slots back to back.
;
; Memory: words 0x001 .. 0x04B are data (the JMP at 0 skips them; only
; DEVICE_INFO, 0x039 .. 0x04B, is loaded with the image), the code follows
; to 0x1E9; the program spans all four quarters, so only thread 0 may be
; started. The buffer holds the first 44 bytes of a request (every request
; this program answers fits) and is rewritten in place into the response.
;
; Readings taken on the open spec questions (2026-11-07): ANSI E1.20 itself
; was not read (the download was refused). Timing from the Open Lighting
; Project's documentation, which quotes E1.20 tables 3-1 to 3-4; packet
; layout, PIDs and NACK codes from its source code. Secondary throughout.
;   A partial responder: E1.20 also requires SUPPORTED_PARAMETERS,
;   SOFTWARE_VERSION_LABEL and DMX_START_ADDRESS (from memory), which
;   this program NACKs as unknown; 22 words are left.
;   Unchecked: where the responder delay is measured from, the order of
;   the 0xAA and 0x55 halves of each encoded UID byte, and the section
;   numbers in the comments. The DE timing rule is this program's own.
;   Dimmer data is not passed to the host.

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 0
        .pins   RX = IN0, TX = OUT0, DE = OUT1, IDENT = OUT2
        .tick   25                      ; eight ticks a bit at 250 kbit/s
        .equ    OVS = 8                 ; ticks per bit
        .equ    BRKT = 175              ; ticks of low run that make a break
        .equ    ISTO = 4200 + 12        ; ticks from a first stop bit's middle:
                                        ; 2.1 ms of mark after the slot, at most
        .equ    DELAY = 404             ; ticks from the last stop bit's middle
        .equ    BRKH = 184              ; half the response's break, in ticks
        .equ    MABT = 32               ; the response's mark after break
        .equ    BUF = 0x001             ; the packet, byte i at BUF + i
        .equ    BUFN = 44               ; bytes kept
        .equ    UID = 0x02D             ; the UID, 6 bytes MSB first
        .equ    CSUM = 0x033            ; then the DUB checksum, 2 bytes
        .equ    MUTED = 0x035
        .equ    IDENTW = 0x036
        .equ    TXAT = 0x037            ; the tick the response starts at
        .equ    PIDW = 0x038            ; the request's PID, for the report
        .equ    DEVINFO = 0x039         ; DEVICE_INFO's 19 bytes
        .equ    PD = BUF + 24           ; parameter data
        .equ    SENT = 0x01             ; report flags (word 1, bits 7:0)
        .equ    DUBF = 0x02
        .equ    NACKF = 0x04
        .equ    BCASTF = 0x08
        .equ    IDF = 0x10
        .equ    MUTEF = 0x20

        JMP     start
; BUF, UID, CSUM, MUTED, IDENTW, TXAT and PIDW (0x001 .. 0x038) are written
; by the program before it reads them, so the image does not load them.
        .org    DEVINFO
; DEVICE_INFO (E1.20 10.5.1, unchecked): RDM protocol version 1.0; model ID
; 0x0001; product category 0x0000 (not declared); software version ID
; 0x00000001; DMX512 footprint 0; personality 1 of 1; DMX512 start address
; 0xFFFF (no footprint); no sub-devices; no sensors.
        .word   0x01, 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00
        .word   0x00, 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, 0x00, 0x00
        .word   0x01, 0x01, 0xFF, 0xFF, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00

; ------------------------------------------------------------------ start
start:  SETP    TX, 1                   ; mark
        OEP     TX, 1                   ; (no-ops unless moved to BIDIR pins)
        SETP    DE, 0                   ; the driver off: listen
        OEP     DE, 1
        SETP    IDENT, 0
        OEP     IDENT, 1
        .csr    BE_PINS, (pin(RX) << 5) | pin(TX)
        .csr    BE_CFG, 0               ; NRZ, LSB first, no CRC
        LDI     r2, UID
        LDI     r3, 3
uidw:   POP     r0                      ; the UID, a 16-bit word at a time
        MOV     r1, r0
        SHRI    r1, 8
        ST      r1, r2, 0
        SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 8
        ST      r0, r2, 1
        ADDI    r2, 2
        DJNZ    r3, uidw
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r0, r2, MUTED - CSUM    ; r2 = CSUM here: unmuted
        ST      r0, r2, IDENTW - CSUM   ; identify off

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- hunting
; Time every low run until one is a break (Table 3-3: 88 us at least).
hunt:   WAITP   RX, 0                   ; a fall
        CSRR    r6, NOW
; The low run that started at r6 ends.
low:    WAITP   RX, 1
        CSRR    r0, NOW                 ; the rise
        SUB     r1, r0, r6
        LDI     r7, BRKT
        CMP     r1, r7                  ; C = a break
        BNC     hunt

; ------------------------------------------------------------- the packet
; Registers: r0 the byte, r1 scratch, r2 bytes so far, r3 their sum, r4 the
; last two bytes (the checksum, at the end), r5 the message length + 2
; once byte 2 is in (0 before), r6 NOW at the slot's start edge, r7 scratch.
brk:    LDI     r2, 0
        LDI     r3, 0
        LDI     r5, 0
        WAITP   RX, 0                   ; the start code's start bit
slot:   SETD    0                       ; anchor on its edge
        CSRR    r6, NOW                 ; and keep it, to time a break
        WAITD   OVS / 2                 ; the middle of the start bit
        JP      RX, 0, sok
        JMP     hunt                    ; high again: a glitch
sok:    LDI     r1, 8
        CSRW    CNT, r1
sbit:   WAITD   OVS
        SHI                             ; a data bit, LSB first
        BNZ     sbit
        WAITD   OVS                     ; the middle of the first stop bit
        JP      RX, 1, stopok
; The first stop bit is low: a framing error, or a break if the line stays
; low long enough (timed from the slot's start edge, r6, by low).
        JMP     low
stopok: STSR    r0
        SHRI    r0, 8                   ; the byte (SR 15:8)
        CMPI    r2, BUFN
        BC      nost                    ; past the buffer: summed, not kept
        ST      r0, r2, BUF
nost:   CMPI    r2, 3
        BC      sum                     ; the header's first three bytes:
        CMPI    r2, 1
        BZ      hsub
        BC      hlen
        LDI     r1, 0xCC                ; byte 0, the start code: RDM's,
        CMP     r0, r1                  ; or the packet is not ours (DMX512
        BNZ     hunt1                   ; dimmer data, any other start code)
        JMP     sum
hsub:   CMPI    r0, 0x01                ; byte 1: SUB_START_CODE
        BNZ     hunt1
        JMP     sum
hlen:   CMPI    r0, 24                  ; byte 2: the message length, 24 at least
        BNC     hunt1
        MOV     r5, r0
        ADDI    r5, 2                   ; and the checksum after it
sum:    ADD     r3, r3, r0
        SHLI    r4, 8
        OR      r4, r4, r0
        INC     r2
        CMP     r2, r5
        BZ      done
        CSRR    r1, TD                  ; the next start bit within 2.1 ms
        MOV16   r7, ISTO
        ADD     r1, r1, r7
        CSRW    TD, r1
        WAITP   RX, 0, T
        BNT     slot
hunt1:  JMP     hunt                    ; timed out: the packet is dropped

; ------------------------------------------------------------- the request
; The last byte is in. TD is the middle of its first stop bit: the response
; starts DELAY ticks on (TXAT). r3 is the sum of every byte, the checksum's
; two included; r4 the checksum (E1.20 6.2.8: the 16-bit sum of every
; byte from the start code to the parameter data, high byte first).
done:   CSRR    r1, TD
        MOV16   r7, DELAY
        ADD     r1, r1, r7
        LDI     r7, TXAT
        ST      r1, r7, 0
        MOV     r1, r4
        SHRI    r1, 8
        SUB     r3, r3, r1
        MOV     r1, r4
        SHLI    r1, 8
        SHRI    r1, 8
        SUB     r3, r3, r1              ; the sum before the checksum
        CMP     r3, r4
        BNZ     bad1
        LDI     r0, 0
        LD      r1, r0, BUF + 2         ; the message length
        SUBI    r1, 24
        LD      r4, r0, BUF + 23        ; the parameter data length, PDL
        CMP     r1, r4
        BNZ     bad1                    ; the two disagree

; The destination: this UID, or a broadcast (E1.20 5.1: device ID
; 0xFFFFFFFF, manufacturer 0xFFFF for all, or this one's).
        LDI     r6, 0                   ; the report's flags
        LDI     r0, BUF + 3
        LDI     r1, UID
        LDI     r2, 6
dmatch: LD      r3, r0, 0
        LD      r5, r1, 0
        CMP     r3, r5
        BNZ     dbc
        INC     r0
        INC     r1
        DJNZ    r2, dmatch
        JMP     mine
dbc:    LDI     r0, 0
        LD      r3, r0, BUF + 5
        LD      r5, r0, BUF + 6
        AND     r3, r3, r5
        LD      r5, r0, BUF + 7
        AND     r3, r3, r5
        LD      r5, r0, BUF + 8
        AND     r3, r3, r5
        LDI     r5, 0xFF
        CMP     r3, r5
        BNZ     other                   ; another device's packet
        LD      r3, r0, BUF + 3
        LD      r1, r0, BUF + 4
        AND     r2, r3, r1
        CMP     r2, r5
        BZ      isbc                    ; all devices
        LDI     r2, UID
        LD      r5, r2, 0
        CMP     r3, r5
        BNZ     other
        LD      r5, r2, 1
        CMP     r1, r5
        BNZ     other                   ; another manufacturer's devices
isbc:   LDI     r6, BCASTF

; Registers from here: r0 0, r3 the command class, r4 PDL, r5 the PID,
; r6 the report.
mine:   LDI     r0, 0
        LD      r3, r0, BUF + 20        ; the command class
        SWAP    r1, r3
        OR      r6, r6, r1              ; into the report's 15:8
        LD      r5, r0, BUF + 21
        SWAP    r5, r5
        LD      r1, r0, BUF + 22
        OR      r5, r5, r1              ; the parameter ID
        LDI     r1, PIDW
        ST      r5, r1, 0
        CMPI    r3, 0x10                ; DISCOVERY_COMMAND
        BZ      disc
        CMPI    r3, 0x20                ; GET_COMMAND
        BZ      get
        CMPI    r3, 0x30                ; SET_COMMAND
        BZ      set
        JMP     report                  ; another class: not answered
other:  JMP     hunt
bad1:   JMP     bad

; Discovery (E1.20 7): DISC_UNIQUE_BRANCH 0x0001, DISC_MUTE 0x0002,
; DISC_UN_MUTE 0x0003; the last two take no data and answer with a
; control field (7.6.1), 0x0000 here: no proxy, no sub-devices.
disc:   CMPI    r5, 1
        BZ      dub1
        TEST    r4, r4
        BNZ     report1
        LDI     r1, 1                   ; muted
        CMPI    r5, 2
        BZ      mset
        CMPI    r5, 3
        BNZ     report1
        LDI     r1, 0                   ; unmuted
mset:   LDI     r2, MUTED
        ST      r1, r2, 0
        LDI     r1, 0
        ST      r1, r0, PD
        ST      r1, r0, PD + 1
        LDI     r4, 2
        JMP     ack
dub1:   JMP     dub
report1:
        JMP     report

; GET: the root device only (sub-device 0), no parameter data.
get:    LD      r1, r0, BUF + 18
        LD      r2, r0, BUF + 19
        OR      r1, r1, r2
        BNZ     nsub
        TEST    r4, r4
        BNZ     nfmt
        LDI     r1, 0x60                ; DEVICE_INFO
        CMP     r5, r1
        BZ      dinfo
        MOV16   r1, 0x1000              ; IDENTIFY_DEVICE
        CMP     r5, r1
        BNZ     npid
        LDI     r1, IDENTW
        LD      r1, r1, 0
        ST      r1, r0, PD              ; 0 or 1
        LDI     r4, 1
        JMP     ack
dinfo:  LDI     r1, DEVINFO
        LDI     r2, PD
        LDI     r4, 19
dic:    LD      r3, r1, 0
        ST      r3, r2, 0
        INC     r1
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r4, dic
        LDI     r4, 19
        JMP     ack

; SET: the root device, or all of them (0xFFFF), which here is the root.
set:    LD      r1, r0, BUF + 18
        LD      r2, r0, BUF + 19
        AND     r7, r1, r2
        OR      r1, r1, r2
        BZ      sroot
        LDI     r2, 0xFF
        CMP     r7, r2
        BNZ     nsub
sroot:  MOV16   r1, 0x1000              ; IDENTIFY_DEVICE
        CMP     r5, r1
        BZ      sident
        LDI     r1, 0x60                ; DEVICE_INFO cannot be set
        CMP     r5, r1
        BNZ     npid
        LDI     r1, 5                   ; NR_UNSUPPORTED_COMMAND_CLASS
        JMP     nack
sident: CMPI    r4, 1
        BNZ     nfmt                    ; one byte of data
        LD      r1, r0, PD
        CMPI    r1, 2
        BC      nrange                  ; 0 (off) or 1 (on) only
        LDI     r2, IDENTW
        ST      r1, r2, 0
        TEST    r1, r1
        BZ      idoff
        SETP    IDENT, 1
        JMP     idack
idoff:  SETP    IDENT, 0
idack:  LDI     r4, 0
        JMP     ack

nsub:   LDI     r1, 0x09                ; NR_SUB_DEVICE_OUT_OF_RANGE
        JMP     nack
nfmt:   LDI     r1, 0x01                ; NR_FORMAT_ERROR
        JMP     nack
nrange: LDI     r1, 0x06                ; NR_DATA_OUT_OF_RANGE
        JMP     nack
npid:   LDI     r1, 0x00                ; NR_UNKNOWN_PID
nack:   LDI     r2, 0
        ST      r2, r0, PD              ; the reason code, high byte first
        ST      r1, r0, PD + 1
        LDI     r4, 2
        LDI     r3, 2                   ; response type NACK_REASON
        JMP     reply
ack:    LDI     r3, 0                   ; response type ACK

; reply: r3 the response type, r4 PDL, the data at PD. The request becomes
; the response in place: destination <= source, source <= this UID, the
; transaction number, sub-device and PID kept, the command class + 1,
; message count 0.
reply:  MOV     r1, r6
        ANDI    r1, BCASTF
        BNZ     report                  ; a broadcast is never answered
        TEST    r3, r3
        BZ      rack
        ORI     r6, NACKF
rack:   ORI     r6, SENT
        LDI     r0, 0
        ST      r3, r0, BUF + 16        ; response type (the port ID's place)
        ST      r0, r0, BUF + 17        ; message count
        LD      r1, r0, BUF + 20
        INC     r1
        ST      r1, r0, BUF + 20        ; GET_COMMAND_RESPONSE and the like
        ST      r4, r0, BUF + 23
        ADDI    r4, 24
        ST      r4, r0, BUF + 2         ; the message length
        LDI     r0, BUF + 3
        LDI     r1, UID
        LDI     r2, 6
rcp:    LD      r5, r0, 6
        ST      r5, r0, 0
        LD      r5, r1, 0
        ST      r5, r0, 6
        INC     r0
        INC     r1
        DJNZ    r2, rcp
        JMP     txgo

; report: the flags and the PID. TD has passed on every path here (the
; request's last stop bit, or the response's), so each WAITB is a test.
report: LDI     r0, MUTED
        LD      r1, r0, 0
        TEST    r1, r1
        BZ      rp1
        ORI     r6, MUTEF
rp1:    LD      r1, r0, IDENTW - MUTED
        TEST    r1, r1
        BZ      rp2
        ORI     r6, IDF
rp2:    WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T              ; T = 1 only if OUTQ is full
        BT      rdone
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, and only the host takes words out of OUTQ"
        PUSH    r6
        LDI     r1, PIDW
        LD      r1, r1, 0
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T
        BT      rdone
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, and only the host takes words out of OUTQ"
        PUSH    r1
rdone:  JMP     hunt
bad:    LDI     r6, 0x80                ; a bad checksum or length
        WAITB   OUTQ_NF, T
        BT      rdone
        .bounded "the WAITB OUTQ_NF, T just before completed by its condition, and only the host takes words out of OUTQ"
        PUSH    r6
        JMP     hunt

; DISC_UNIQUE_BRANCH (E1.20 7.5): PDL 12, the lower bound then the upper
; bound, each a UID MSB first. Unmuted and lower <= UID <= upper: answer.
dub:    LDI     r1, MUTED
        LD      r1, r1, 0
        TEST    r1, r1
        BNZ     report
        CMPI    r4, 12
        BNZ     report
        LDI     r1, UID                 ; UID >= lower, MSB first
        LDI     r2, PD
        LDI     r4, 6
dlo:    LD      r3, r1, 0
        LD      r5, r2, 0
        CMP     r3, r5                  ; C = (uid byte >= bound byte)
        BNZ     dlo1                    ; they differ: C decides
        INC     r1
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r4, dlo
        JMP     dhi                     ; equal
dlo1:   BNC     report                  ; below the lower bound
dhi:    LDI     r1, PD + 6              ; upper >= UID
        LDI     r2, UID
        LDI     r4, 6
dhl:    LD      r3, r1, 0
        LD      r5, r2, 0
        CMP     r3, r5
        BNZ     dhi1
        INC     r1
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r4, dhl
        JMP     dfill
dhi1:   BNC     report                  ; above the upper bound

; The response: seven 0xFE, 0xAA, then the UID and the sum of its encoded
; bytes, each byte b as b | 0xAA then b | 0x55. CSUM follows UID in memory,
; so one loop of eight encodes both; the sum is stored after six.
dfill:  LDI     r0, BUF
        LDI     r1, 0xFE
        LDI     r2, 7
dpre:   ST      r1, r0, 0
        INC     r0
        DJNZ    r2, dpre
        LDI     r1, 0xAA
        ST      r1, r0, 0
        INC     r0
        LDI     r2, 8
        LDI     r3, 0                   ; the sum of the encoded UID
        LDI     r4, UID
denc:   CMPI    r2, 2
        BNZ     denc1
        MOV     r1, r3                  ; the UID is done: CSUM <= the sum
        SHRI    r1, 8
        ST      r1, r4, 0
        SHLI    r3, 8
        SHRI    r3, 8
        ST      r3, r4, 1
denc1:  LD      r1, r4, 0
        INC     r4
        LDI     r5, 0xAA
        OR      r5, r5, r1
        ST      r5, r0, 0
        ADD     r3, r3, r5
        LDI     r5, 0x55
        OR      r5, r5, r1
        ST      r5, r0, 1
        ADD     r3, r3, r5
        ADDI    r0, 2
        DJNZ    r2, denc
        ORI     r6, DUBF
        LDI     r4, 24

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- respond
; r4 bytes from BUF, then the checksum high byte first, except after a DUB
; response, which carries its own. Every pin write is the instruction
; right after the WAITD that times it, so every edge lands the same few
; clocks after its tick.
txgo:   LDI     r1, TXAT
        LD      r1, r1, 0
        CSRW    TD, r1
        WAITD   0                       ; until TXAT
        SETD    0                       ; and anchor there
        SETP    DE, 1                   ; drive the line
        LDI     r1, 0
        LDIH    r1, 6                   ; r1 = 0x0600: the stop bits
        LDI     r2, BUF
        LDI     r3, 0                   ; the checksum
        MOV     r0, r6
        ANDI    r0, DUBF
        BNZ     txl                     ; a DUB response has no break
        WAITD   OVS
        SETP    TX, 0                   ; break
        WAITD   BRKH
        WAITD   BRKH
        SETP    TX, 1                   ; mark after break
        WAITD   MABT - OVS              ; the start bit one bit on, in txb
txl:    LD      r0, r2, 0
        ADD     r3, r3, r0
        CALL    txb
        INC     r2
        DJNZ    r4, txl
        MOV     r0, r6
        ANDI    r0, DUBF
        BNZ     txend
        MOV     r0, r3
        SHRI    r0, 8
        CALL    txb                     ; the checksum's high byte
        MOV     r0, r3
        SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 8
        CALL    txb                     ; and its low byte
txend:  WAITD   OVS                     ; the end of the last stop bit
        SETP    DE, 0                   ; release the line
        JMP     report

; txb: one 8N2 slot of the byte in r0 (bits 15:8 zero), its start bit OVS
; ticks after TD. SR holds {stop, stop, data 7:0, start}, CNT = 11; the
; eleventh SHO is the second stop bit. The only CALLed routine: the
; deadline checker sends every RET to every CALL site.
txb:    SHLI    r0, 8
        SHRI    r0, 7                   ; data in 8:1, the start bit 0 in bit 0
        OR      r0, r0, r1              ; the stop bits
        LDSR    r0
        LDI     r0, 11
        CSRW    CNT, r0
tbit:   WAITD   OVS
        SHO                             ; Z = (CNT == 0): the slot is out
        BNZ     tbit
        RET
